Kora PayNet – Project Guidelines (V1)
1. Vision & Core Idea

Kora PayNet bridges the gap between cryptocurrencies and everyday users.
Our mission is to make crypto:

Easily accessible (anyone can top up using crypto).

Borderless (users can send it instantly anywhere in the world).

Locally usable (recipients can withdraw into their local cash via Merchants/P2P).

👉 In short: Top up with crypto → Send globally → Withdraw in cash locally.
This is our unique differentiator compared to other fintech wallets.

2. Core Features (V1)
User Side (Basic Users)

Sign up & Wallet Setup

Simple onboarding (email/phone + KYC-lite for compliance if needed).

Each user gets a multi-crypto wallet (BTC, ETH, USDT) local currency(For pairing the prices only) EXample(RWF).

Top-up Options

Add crypto from external wallets/exchanges into Kora PayNet wallet.

In-app QR code & wallet address copy for deposits.

Send & Receive Transfers

Instant transfers between PayNet users (no blockchain fee).

Option to send via username, phone, or QR code.

Withdraw (via Merchants / P2P)

User selects “Withdraw to Cash.”

System auto-matches them with a Merchant (P2P) offering local cash-out at their chosen rate.

Optional System Tips

After successful transactions, user can “tip” the system (voluntary contribution).

Merchant Side (P2P Facilitators)

Merchant Requirements

Must invite 5 users.

Must pay subscription fee to be verified.

Merchant Services

Can offer:

Cash-out (withdraw crypto to local currency)

Cash-in (sell crypto for local deposits, if allowed)

Visibility & Ranking

Verified merchants only.

Boost/visibility fee option to appear in top results.

Matching System

Auto-matching users to merchants based on:

Rate competitiveness.

Merchant reliability/verification status.

Sponsored/boosted merchants (system priority).

3. Monetization Model (V1)

We stay user-first and not profit-hungry. Revenue comes from:

Merchant subscription fee.

Merchant visibility/boost fees.

Optional user tips.

Virtual cards (for spending crypto directly, Phase 1.5).

4. UI/UX Guidelines

Design Language:

Clean, global fintech style (like CashApp / Binance Lite).

Colors:Blue (#2B6CB0) → conveys trust, stability, and reliability.

Green (#38A169) → represents growth, prosperity, and money.

Dark Gray/Black (#1A202C) → adds contrast, professionalism, and authority.

White (#FFFFFF) → background for clarity and simplicity.

Flows to Design First:

Onboarding & Wallet setup.

Crypto Top-up flow.

Send/receive money flow.

Withdraw via merchant flow.

Merchant dashboard & visibility options.

Principle: Zero learning curve. If a grandma in a village opens it, she must understand “Send → Receive → Withdraw.”

